-- The machine's composition rule opens a family at a fresh dimension and,
-- by its head, applies one of the %comp-* clauses below to the family's
-- components as lines. A tube is a system of lines; transformations of a
-- tube act branchwise with sysmap.
-- Read clause by clause on 2026-11-12 against CCHM (Cohen, Coquand, Huber, Mörtberg, “Cubical Type
-- Theory: a constructive interpretation of the univalence axiom”, TYPES 2015, arXiv:1611.02108:
-- fill §4.4 “Kan filling operation”, composition at Π, Σ and paths §4.5 “Equality judgments for composition”,
-- transport §4.6 “Transport”, Glue §6.2 “Composition for glueing” and appendix A “Details of composition for glueing”), the
-- HIT eliminator on hcomp (Coquand, Huber, Mörtberg, LICS 2018) and, for the universe, Cubical
-- Agda (Vezzosi, Mörtberg, Abel). The papers are not in this repository and could not be fetched
-- here; the reading is against their rules as the reader knows them, recorded at each clause.
-- Result: fill, transp, hcomp, %comp-pi, %comp-sigma, %comp-path, %comp-glue and %case-hcomp are
-- those rules; %comp-u, %unglue-line, %tproof and %comp-gluel follow Cubical Agda's composition of
-- types as a type former instead of CCHM §7.1 “Composition for the universe”; the language implementation goal records this.
--
-- universe levels: U carries its level; lomega is the level of types quantifying over levels
data Level = lzero | lsuc (l : Level) | lmax (a : Level) (b : Level) | lomega
